th1-surjection-curation-001+math1-bijection-curation-001+math1-union-curation-001+math1-proper-curation-001+math1-complement-curation-001+math1-complement-render-001+math1-division-curation-001+math1-reciprocal-curation-001+math1-inequality-curation-001+math1-inequality-feedback-001+math1-maximum-curation-001+math1-minimum-curation-001+math1-boundedset-curation-001+math1-endpoint-curation-001+audit-groups-20261027+topup-math-i-20261028+topup-math-ii-20261028+topup-pt-20261028+topup-math-iii-20261028","concept_id":"Year-1/1b-Math-II-Linear-Algebra/homogeneous-system.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-1/1b-Math-II-Linear-Algebra/homogeneous-system.html","questions":[{"id":"la_batch6_homogeneous_system_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What condition makes a linear system $Ax=b$ homogeneous?","options":["All entries of $A$ are positive.","$b=0$.","$x=0$ is the only possible vector.","$A=0$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"53deecd05037dfc4d29cb628","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch6_homogeneous_system_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why does every homogeneous system have at least one solution?","options":["$x=0$ always satisfies $Ax=0$.","The right-hand side can be chosen after solving.","Every homogeneous system has every vector as a solution.","The coefficient matrix must be invertible."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2539263ed179afdc1786a926","time_limit":25},{"id":"la_batch6_homogeneous_system_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If a homogeneous system has more unknowns than independent equations, what often appears in its solution description?","options":["Free parameters leading to nontrivial solutions.","A unique right-hand side chosen after solving.","A nonzero right-hand side vector.","A contradiction of the form $0=1$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8dddb2b0448a59cc06cb6979","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch6_homogeneous_system_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How is the solution set of $Ax=0$ related to the kernel of $A$?","options":["They are the same set of vectors.","The kernel contains only the rows of $A$.","The solution set is the range of $A$.","The kernel is the right-hand side vector."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1d57d3fdff84e097b1879f6b","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch6_homogeneous_system_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Solve the homogeneous system $x+y=0$ and $x-y=0$.","options":["All pairs with $y=-x$.","All pairs with $x=y$.","No solution.","Only $(x,y)=(0,0)$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"cfd9453aa5cdbd008b3f1de8","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch6_homogeneous_system_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\end{pmatrix}$, what is one nontrivial solution of $Ax=0$?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}$ only","$\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}-2\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"85b4825fe198974eae26aafe","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch6_homogeneous_system_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"If $Ax=0$ has a nonzero solution, what does that say about the columns of $A$?","options":["They must all be zero columns.","They must form the standard basis.","They all have the same length.","They satisfy a nontrivial linear relation."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2d9a8bb7df3e01e434acaed6","time_limit":40},{"id":"la_batch6_homogeneous_system_009_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"A homogeneous system $\\boldsymbol{A}\\boldsymbol{x}=\\boldsymbol{0}$ over $\\mathbb{R}$ has a solution $\\boldsymbol{u}\\ne\\boldsymbol{0}$. How many solutions does it have?","options":["Infinitely many: $t\\boldsymbol{u}$ is a solution for every real $t$.","Exactly two: $\\boldsymbol{0}$ and $\\boldsymbol{u}$.","Exactly three: $\\boldsymbol{0}$, $\\boldsymbol{u}$ and $-\\boldsymbol{u}$.","Infinitely many only if $\\boldsymbol{A}$ has more columns than rows."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0c03a357b39403f37dfe4b3e","time_limit":35},{"id":"la_batch6_homogeneous_system_019_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"The vector $\\boldsymbol{x}_p=(3,0)$ solves $x_1+2x_2=3$, and the solutions of $x_1+2x_2=0$ are the multiples $t(-2,1)$. Which set is the full solution set of $x_1+2x_2=3$?","options":["$\\{(3,0)+t(-2,1)\\colon t\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}$","$\\{t(-2,1)\\colon t\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}$","$\\{(3,0)+t(1,2)\\colon t\\in\\mathbb{R}\\}$","$\\{(3,0)\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"85e45995e0d4805d2a290ed0","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch6_homogeneous_system_020_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"The reduced form of a homogeneous system in the variables $x,y,z$ is $x+2z=0$, $y-z=0$. Which parametrisation describes all solutions?","options":["$x=2t$, $y=-t$, $z=t$, $t\\in\\mathbb{R}$","$x=-2t$, $y=t$, $z=t$, $t\\in\\mathbb{R}$","$x=t$, $y=t$, $z=-2t$, $t\\in\\mathbb{R}$","$x=0$, $y=0$, $z=0$ only"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1b1c589e714c714e1acfa53e","time_limit":40}]}}